<title>FRANCE: Carrefour buys 33.34 pct of GMB.</title>
<headline>Carrefour buys 33.34 pct of GMB.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>French retail group Carrefour said on Wednesday that it had bought 33.34 percent of the company GMB, which controls the Groupe Cora.</p>
<p>It bought the stake from a group of family shareholders of GMB. The price of the transaction was not announced.</p>
<p>Cora owns 55 hypermarkets and 140 supermarkets and has total annual sales of around 35 billion francs ($6.7 billion).</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ($ = 5.223 French Francs)</p>
